  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "All angles of a square are \\(90^\\circ\\), and the ratios of corresponding side lengths are equal throughout, so squares are necessarily similar. Rectangles and rhombuses satisfy only one of the conditions of equal angles or equal sides, so they are not necessarily similar. D lacks the condition that the sides are proportional.",
